      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Ben,\n\nThis approach doesn\u0027t work if we want to disable one of the multiple ports (for future devices). So, it is more like a workaround (or hack). This solution is handy because it won\u0027t require any host change but I don\u0027t think it deserves a new CONFIG macro.\n\nI suggest we introduce board_get_pchg_count instead and make pchg_task call board_get_pchg_count once on start-up (and save it internally in \u0027static int pchg_count\u0027). Other boards can simply return ARRAY_SIZE(pchgs). This also guarantees pchg_count won\u0027t change once pchg_task starts.\n\n--- \u003e8 ---\n\nI believe the right apporach is to make the kernel check the presence of each port in cros_pchg_probe by calling EC_CMD_PCHG. Then, the kernel automatically disable the module if there is no port availabe (num_registered_psy \u003d\u003d 0).",
